From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenAI <noreply@openai.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: realtek: add bounded RD05 detect boot markers

The v38.1 hardware log stops after MTD registration and before the first
RTL8367D or RTL8197F Ethernet message. Add two non-invasive markers around
the RTL8365MB-family chip-ID transaction so a serial log distinguishes a
hang before SMI detection from one inside the ID read. No switch register
programming or timing is changed.

Signed-off-by: OpenAI <noreply@openai.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb.c
@@ -3328,12 +3328,16 @@
 	int ret;
 	int i;
 
+	dev_info(priv->dev, "RD05 bootstage v38.2: RTL8367 detect enter\n");
 	ret = rtl8365mb_get_chip_id_and_ver(priv->map, &chip_id, &chip_ver);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(priv->dev, "failed to read chip id and version: %d\n",
 			ret);
 		return ret;
 	}
+	dev_info(priv->dev,
+		 "RD05 bootstage v38.2: RTL8367 id=0x%04x ver=0x%04x\n",
+		 chip_id, chip_ver);
 
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(rtl8365mb_chip_infos); i++) {
 		const struct rtl8365mb_chip_info *ci = &rtl8365mb_chip_infos[i];
